  "transport_hash_interpretation": "Every original/reproduction ranking JSONL pair has a different raw SHA-256 because latency_ms is serialized and local timing changed. Exhaustive field comparison found no difference in query_id, query text, product_id, model_id, score, rank, source_index, or ESCI label. The unequal raw transport hashes therefore do not contradict the equal semantic rank-and-score hashes.",
  "limitations": [
    "Both scoring processes ran in a dirty shared worktree. The second process recorded a Git SHA, but that SHA does not identify the uncommitted source state; this is not clean-checkout or commit-bound reproduction evidence.",
    "The second scoring run was a separate process, not a controlled latency experiment. Offline p95 changed by 9.98% to 56.13% across systems, so latency reproducibility is not claimed.",
    "Latency is uncontrolled local offline model-inference timing apportioned to query groups, not AWS Lambda or public API latency.",
    "The original wrapper failed only after all six rankings were complete because of an obsolete report candidate-count cap; the recovery process checksum-reverified the completed rankings before reporting metrics.",
    "The held-out test split was not loaded or evaluated. This evidence makes no candidate-training, held-out, cloud-service, promotion, deployment, or shopper-impact claim."
  ]
